=== The medium/dyad needs g_p ~ 2.8 (strong, > g_c=2) to condense at tau=T_c/m_e~0.34. ===
    Write down EVERY fundamental interaction the model contains, compute the pairing g_p each gives:

  (1) EM photon exchange: alpha=1/137. Between like charges it is REPULSIVE -> does not pair.
      Even taken attractive: g ~ 4 alpha/pi^2 = 0.0030  << 2
  (2) Dark coupling alpha_c=3alpha: g ~ 4 alpha_c/pi^2 = 0.0089  << 2
  (3) Majoron exchange g_Maj~1.2e-8: g ~ N g_Maj^2/pi^2 ~ 5.8e-17  << 2
  (4) eps-fitted kappa=1.09e-13 eV^-2 (from eps=1.24%): the SAME coupling that sets varying-m_e
      -> dyad-exchange pairing g ~ N kappa^2 m_e^4/(pi^2 m_dyad^2) = 2.8e-15  << 2

=== ALL of the model's interactions are WEAK (g << g_c=2), by 2 to 15 orders. ===
    The strong g_p~2.8 the DE value needs is supplied by NONE of them.

=== The framings, and why tau is not derivable in ANY of them ===
  - Composite (NJL/BCS, what we built): needs strong g_p~2.8; NO model coupling supplies it
    -> requires a NEW strong pairing sector, absent from the corpus.
  - Fundamental scalar (tree potential): tau = (dyad bare mass)/m_e -> a FREE parameter, not derived.
  - Radiative CW (the model's stated mechanism, weak eps-kappa): ill-defined/marginal (hunt 215),
    and the eps-fitted kappa gives g~1e-15 -- nowhere near condensation.

=== VERDICT (the honest foundation) ===
Writing down the medium's fundamental interaction shows the model has NO strong sector: every
coupling (alpha, alpha_c, Majoron, the eps-fit kappa) is weak. So g_p ~ 2.8 -- hence tau, hence the
DE-value digit -- is NOT derivable from the existing content. It is either a FREE parameter (if the
dyad is a fundamental scalar) or needs NEW strong physics (if it is a composite). This is a genuine
GAP in the model's foundation: the medium's strong condensation is ASSUMED, not sourced by any
specified interaction. The DE value stands at (d/2)alpha^4 m_e (0.966x, conjecture tau=1/d); its
digit rests on physics the model does not yet contain -- an honest open foundation, not a computation.
